# interplay_fifo_delete_exec_pending: Deleting a child FIFO whose exec was read: the exec was pushed before the delete's quiesce, so DeviceCore::delete_fifo drains it: the fill lands, child 1 publishes its stamp, and only then does the delete's stamp publish. Child 1 is then defined again over a fresh ring and carries an exec on the same task (in the service, the task was told the FIFO was deleted and is sent the new FIFO's event): it copies what the first one wrote.
